From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:42:04 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] asahi: accept the "aurora" kernel driver name

The AGX kernel driver is being renamed from "asahi" to "aurora". Mesa has
to know the new name before any kernel ships with it, otherwise the GL
driver, Borealis and everything on Zink lose the GPU. This accepts both
names everywhere Mesa matches the kernel driver, so Mesa and the kernel
can update in either order.

- agx_device and hk use agx_is_native_drm_driver(), which takes either
  name. The 0.2 version rule for render_rsrc_spec_hi belongs to the old
  numbering and now applies to "asahi" only. The field has no users.
- kmsro pairs the display-only "apple" device with an "aurora" or
  "asahi" render node, and the pipe-loader platform list carries both.
- New "aurora" pipe-loader descriptor for the AGX screen, the same alias
  pattern as msm and kgsl, and dril builds aurora_dri.so beside
  asahi_dri.so.
- The gallium driver's driconf name is now "aurora". A new optional
  driverNameAlias in driConfigFileParseParams lets it keep matching
  <device driver="asahi">, so the drirc files on our systems and option
  names like asahi_no_fp16 keep working. Covered by a new xmlconfig
  test.
- The v3d simulator knows the new name too.

MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE and dri_driver accept "aurora" and "asahi".
Nothing else changes for an "asahi" kernel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6edf62bcfd026b0bf370007d18a59e0205ba6d89)
